1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:03,933
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition Eighteen.

2
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:08,220
In any triangle, the greater side subtends the greater angle.

3
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:16,090
Given triangle A B C with side A C greater than side A B, we prove that angle A B C is greater than angle B C A.

4
00:00:16,510 --> 00:00:22,817
Since side A C is greater than A B, cut off segment A D from A C equal to A B.

5
00:00:22,817 --> 00:00:25,000
Then construct segment B D.

6
00:00:25,420 --> 00:00:32,706
Since angle A D B is an exterior angle of triangle B C D, it is greater than the interior and opposite angle D C B.

7
00:00:32,706 --> 00:00:41,640
Yet because A B equals A D in isosceles triangle A B D, base angle A D B equals angle A B D, so angle A B D is also greater than angle A C B.

8
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:49,940
Since the whole angle A B C is greater than its part A B D, angle A B C is much greater than angle B C A, as was required to prove.
